# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# O.R.I.O.N. — what must never leave this machine.
#
# The rule here is DENY BY DEFAULT for anything ORION writes at runtime.
# An earlier version of this file named each offender individually, which meant
# every new kind of runtime artefact (a browser profile, a crash report, a
# research dossier) arrived un-ignored and one `git add .` away from being
# published. `config/` is now ignored wholesale with a short allowlist of the
# few files that are genuinely source.
#
# NOTE: .gitignore does NOT apply to files git already tracks. If something
# personal is still tracked, `git rm --cached <path>` it — the pattern alone
# will not remove it from the current index or from older commits.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1. Secrets and credentials
**/*api_keys*.json
config/messaging.json
config/remote_secret.key
config/remote_devices.json
*.env
**/.env*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.jks
*.keystore

# 2. Runtime config — deny by default, then allow back the source files.
#    (Covers databases, identity, cognitive state, browser profile, crash
#    reports, self-repair proposals, forged-tool output, caches and anything
#    added in future.)
config/*
!config/knowledge_packs/
config/knowledge_packs/*
!config/knowledge_packs/ai.json
!config/knowledge_packs/business.json
!config/knowledge_packs/coding.json
!config/knowledge_packs/copywriting.json
!config/knowledge_packs/dropshipping.json
!config/knowledge_packs/entrepreneurship.json
!config/knowledge_packs/marketing.json
!config/knowledge_packs/personal_development.json
!config/knowledge_packs/sales_psychology.json
!config/knowledge_packs/tiktok_shop.json
!config/custom_tools/
config/custom_tools/*
# The numbers ORION is allowed to dial. The TEMPLATE is published so a
# fresh checkout knows the shape; the filled-in copy never is, because
# `config/*` above already excludes everything not named here.
!config/telephony_contacts.example.json
!config/custom_tools/__init__.py
!config/custom_tools/discord_message_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/discord_message.plugin.json
!config/custom_tools/telegram_message_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/telegram_message.plugin.json
!config/custom_tools/json_validator_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/json_validator.plugin.json
!config/custom_tools/live_camera_analysis_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/live_camera_analysis.plugin.json
# Plugins that SHIP with ORION, as opposed to ones he forged or the user
# wrote. Everything under config/custom_tools is excluded above because that
# directory is mostly generated; these are part of the application and
# a fresh checkout is missing capabilities without them.
!config/custom_tools/open_meteo_weather_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/open_meteo_weather.plugin.json
!config/custom_tools/push_notify_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/push_notify.plugin.json
!config/custom_tools/philips_hue_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/philips_hue.plugin.json
!config/custom_tools/ifttt_webhook_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/ifttt_webhook.plugin.json
!config/custom_tools/homeassistant_call_service_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/homeassistant_call_service.plugin.json

# 3. Private conversation, research and generated output
conversations/
research/
exports/
reports/
*log*.txt
conversation_log.txt
**/*.jsonl

# 4. Databases and knowledge graphs (memory, location history)
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite3

# 5. Voice recordings and audio
audio_studio/raw/
audio_studio/processed/
audio_studio/packages/
**/*.wav

# 6. Build output and packaged applications
#    Installed copies may contain private runtime configuration.
dist/
# Root only. Unanchored, this matched ANY directory named 'build' at any
# depth — including assets/three/build/, which silently kept the vendored
# WebGL library out of the repository and left ORION streaming his own
# face from a CDN.
/build/
# Whole projects ORION has written for himself. His output,
# not his source.
/projects/
ORION.exe
release/
*.exe
*.dll
*.pyd
*.apk
*.aab
*.spec

# 7. Python environment and caches
venv/
.venv/
env/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
/.test-tmp*/

# 8. Editor, OS and tooling artefacts
#    .claude/ holds local agent tooling config (launch.json carries absolute
#    home paths and other projects' locations) — it was deliberately removed
#    from this repo once already.
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
*.rej
*.orig
*.bak
*.utf16.bak
*.log
recursive_file_list.txt
/PLANS.md

# 9. Office lock/temp files and generated documents
~$*
*.docx
!docs/**/*.docx

# 10. Reviewed plugins that ship with ORION (see PUBLIC_CONFIG_FILES in
#     tools/prepare_public_source.py). They sit under the ignored
#     config/custom_tools/ like forged tools, but are part of the application.
!config/custom_tools/emotional_monitor_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/emotional_monitor.plugin.json
!config/custom_tools/error_handler_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/error_handler.plugin.json
!config/custom_tools/synthesis_enhancer_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/synthesis_enhancer.plugin.json
!config/custom_tools/fitness_goal_tracker_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/fitness_goal_tracker.plugin.json
!config/custom_tools/fitness_progress_monitor_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/fitness_progress_monitor.plugin.json
!config/custom_tools/dependency_manager_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/dependency_manager.plugin.json
!config/custom_tools/dependency_resolver_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/dependency_resolver.plugin.json
!config/custom_tools/emotional_insight_generator_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/emotional_insight_generator.plugin.json
!config/custom_tools/self_repair_agent_tool.py
!config/custom_tools/self_repair_agent.plugin.json
